<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Capsus</h1><p class="st-meta">500 CE – 548 CE (approx.) · capital Capsa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Berber principality of southern Tunisia under Antalas, who fought the Vandals, allied with Byzantium and then turned against it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the early 6th century, as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vandal-kingdom">Vandal Kingdom</a> lost control of the interior, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> chiefs of the Frexes and neighbouring tribes built a power base in southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/byzacena">Byzacena</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gafsa">Capsa</a> (Gafsa). Its best-known leader, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antalas">Antalas</a>, son of Guenfan, defeated a Vandal army sent by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hilderic">Hilderic</a> around 530.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>What is known comes from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/procopius">Procopius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corippus">Corippus</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antalas">Antalas</a> led a tribal confederation of herders and oasis farmers on the desert edge. He sided with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> after their conquest of 533 to 534, receiving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subsidy">subsidies</a>, but rebelled in 544 after the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> executed his brother. That year his forces killed Solomon at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cillium">Cillium</a>, and he briefly allied with the Byzantine mutineer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stotzas">Stotzas</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antalas">Antalas</a> was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-troglita">John Troglita</a>, the general of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/praetorian-prefecture-of-africa">Praetorian Prefecture of Africa</a>, and submitted around 546 to 548, fighting thereafter as a Byzantine ally against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/laguatan">Laguatan</a>. His principality then disappears from the record.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-capsus.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Capsus" width="320" height="238"><figcaption>Image: Naslechat · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Romano-Berber_Kingdoms.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 CE – 548 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Capsa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Antalas</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Berber religion, Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Berber</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/tunisia">Tunisia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Antalas, Frexes</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=524&amp;focus=kingdom-of-capsus" aria-label="Kingdom of Capsus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4911 948 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Capsus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5259 1106h0M5259 1106h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5231 1204h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5231 1204h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Tunisia. <a href="/atlas?year=524&amp;focus=kingdom-of-capsus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
